                <pb facs="0880" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3999: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-05T11:00:00+00:00">December 5, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Queipo de Llano promised to inform General Franco of the contents of the
                    Department’s [December?] 3, 5 p.m. which I communicated to him last night. On
                    that occasion he stated Russian merchantmen were flying flags of other countries
                    and on one occasion flew the American flag while in Spanish waters. He stated
                    also that a Russian submarine is known to be operating along the Spanish coast.
                    These comments were offered apparently to convey an idea of the lawless tactics
                    against which they are contending.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
